<title>NORWAY: Norway says monetary policy unchanged.</title>
<headline>Norway says monetary policy unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Norwegian government said in its draft 1997 budget on Friday that its monetary and exchange rate policy was unchanged and aimed at maintaining a stable crown.</p>
<p>&quot;Monetary and exchange rate policy is oriented towards maintaining a stable crown exchange rate against European currencies as a means to achieve low price and wage inflation,&quot; a statement said.</p>
<p>Norway abandoned the crown's formal link to the European Currency Unit (ECU) in 1992 and has since maintained a so-called dirty float.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
